welcome to CBS this morning we begin  with breaking news about a suspected  chemical weapons attack in Syria it  could be among the deadliest in the  Civil War the reported attack took place  in a rebel health section of Idlib  province in northwestern Syria a warning  video of the aftermath is disturbing  what a but it will be important evidence  as investigators try to confirm whether  chemical weapons were used syrian  activists say at least 58 people were  killed and dozens wounded they blame the  Syrian government or Russian jets Holly  Williams is in Istanbul Turkey Holly  good morning good morning we are still  working to independently confirm whether  this was a chemical attack but the video  is emerging from Syria today certainly  suggests that some kind of chemical  agent was used against civilians  including children we are not airing  some of the most disturbing videos but  this one apparently from the immediate  aftermath appears to show those who were  injured and killed without any visible  wounds those still alive appear to be  having respiratory problems in a clinic  where doctors treat multiple patients in  one video a doctor shows that his  patients pupils are not responding to  light all of that according to a  chemical weapons expert and CBS  contributor is consistent with exposure  to a nerve agent now a blue province is  a stronghold for Syrian rebels and it's  been pounded by Syrian regime and  Russian airstrikes but at this point we  cannot confirm who carried out this  attack in August 2013 a rebel-held area  close to the Syrian capital Damascus  was hit by rockets containing sarin  nerve agent hundreds of people are  thought to have died in that attack the  US and several of its key allies blamed  this Syrian regime gaile all right Holly  those images very tough to see thank you  very much reporting from Istanbul
 

